{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgArWHAyq3vGnG61qpezE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JtunS7XCbw4JFi6gSViPBB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-Fpfs5S; sed -i '' -e 's|claude -p \"\\$PROMPT\" --output-format text > \"\\$OUT\"|claude -p \"$PROMPT\" --output-format text < /dev/null > \"$OUT\"|' -e 's|^status=\\$?|rc=$?|' -e 's|\\$status|$rc|g' bin/nightly-review.zsh\nsed -i '' 's|^  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>|&|; /<key>EnvironmentVariables<\\/key>/{n;s|<dict>|<dict>\\\n    <key>USER</key>\\\n    <string>vk</string>\\\n    <key>HOME</key>\\\n    <string>/Users/vk</string>|;}' Library/LaunchAgents/*.plist\nplutil -lint Library/LaunchAgents/*.plist; zsh -n bin/nightly-review.zsh; sed -n 17,28p bin/nightly-review.zsh\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Why nightly-review was silent\n\nThe job did run (launchctl print: `runs = 6`, `last exit code = 1`). It failed, and the failure reporter died too. The cause is two stacked bugs, visible in `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`.\n\n1. **`claude` fails with \"Not logged in\".** launchd gives the job no `USER` (or `HOME`) in its environment, so the CLI can't find its login in the keychain. The review exits non-zero every night.\n2. **`status=$?` in `bin/nightly-review.zsh` is fatal in zsh.** `status` is a read-only builtin, so the script dies with `read-only variable: status`. That happens before the `notify.sh` failure call, so no failure note is ever sent.\n\nTogether these meant no summary and no failure message.\n\n## Fixes\n- Script: `status` → `rc`. Also added `< /dev/null` to the `claude -p` call so it can't wait on stdin.\n- Plist: added `USER=vk` and `HOME=/Users/vk` under `EnvironmentVariables`.\n\n## To apply and verify\nThe plist is loaded in launchd, so reload it:\n`launchctl bootout gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review; launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist; launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`\n\nThen check that you get the Telegram message and that the run takes a plausible time. I couldn't run any of this here.\n\n## Not verified\n- `claude` has to be on the plist PATH (`/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:...`). If it lives in `~/.local/bin`, add that to PATH.\n- `notify.sh` reads its token from the keychain, which should work in the gui domain.\n- Changes are in this snapshot only. Copy them to your real home dir.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":631,"cache_read_input_tokens":23932,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":631},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23bd704c-bda7-484f-9483-74d77cb24b73","uuid":"a300461a-abd5-4f68-9057-8a011f1c4c22","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:04:35.416Z","request_id":"req_011CgArWGvMP6cfYkfJ8be9v","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JtunS7XCbw4JFi6gSViPBB":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-Fpfs5S; sed -i '' -e 's|claude -p \"\\$PROMPT\" --output-format text > \"\\$OUT\"|claude -p \"$PROMPT\" --output-format text < /dev/null > \"$OUT\"|' -e 's|^status=\\$?|rc=$?|' -e 's|\\$status|$rc|g' bin/nightly-review.zsh\nsed -i '' 's|^  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>|&|; /<key>EnvironmentVariables<\\/key>/{n;s|<dict>|<dict>\\\n    <key>USER</key>\\\n    <string>vk</string>\\\n    <key>HOME</key>\\\n    <string>/Users/vk</string>|;}' Library/LaunchAgents/*.plist\nplutil -lint Library/LaunchAgents/*.plist; zsh -n bin/nightly-review.zsh; sed -n 17,28p bin/nightly-review.zsh\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Why nightly-review was silent\n\nThe job did run (launchctl print: `runs = 6`, `last exit code = 1`). It failed, and the failure reporter died too. The cause is two stacked bugs, visible in `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`.\n\n1. **`claude` fails with \"Not logged in\".** launchd gives the job no `USER` (or `HOME`) in its environment, so the CLI can't find its login in the keychain. The review exits non-zero every night.\n2. **`status=$?` in `bin/nightly-review.zsh` is fatal in zsh.** `status` is a read-only builtin, so the script dies with `read-only variable: status`. That happens before the `notify.sh` failure call, so no failure note is ever sent.\n\nTogether these meant no summary and no failure message.\n\n## Fixes\n- Script: `status` → `rc`. Also added `< /dev/null` to the `claude -p` call so it can't wait on stdin.\n- Plist: added `USER=vk` and `HOME=/Users/vk` under `EnvironmentVariables`.\n\n## To apply and verify\nThe plist is loaded in launchd, so reload it:\n`launchctl bootout gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review; launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist; launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`\n\nThen check that you get the Telegram message and that the run takes a plausible time. I couldn't run any of this here.\n\n## Not verified\n- `claude` has to be on the plist PATH (`/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:...`). If it lives in `~/.local/bin`, add that to PATH.\n- `notify.sh` reads its token from the keychain, which should work in the gui domain.\n- Changes are in this snapshot only. Copy them to your real home dir.\nE"}}}
