{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgArXFx62AyZWwyfDrucM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found two bugs that stacked on each other, and I fixed both in this folder. I couldn't run launchd or `claude` here, so none of it has been tested.\n\nThe job did run: `launchctl print` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`. It failed every night, and the failure note never got sent. `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err` shows both bugs.\n\n1. **`claude` fails with \"Not logged in\".** launchd doesn't give the job `USER` or `HOME`, so the CLI can't find its login in the keychain.\n2. **`status=$?` kills the script.** In zsh `status` is read-only, so the script dies with `read-only variable: status`. That happens before the `notify.sh` failure call, so you never got a failure message.\n\n**Fixes**\n- In `bin/nightly-review.zsh`, `status` is now `rc`. I also added `< /dev/null` to the `claude -p` call so it can't wait on stdin.\n- In the plist, I added `USER=vk` and `HOME=/Users/vk` under `EnvironmentVariables`.\n\n**To apply**\n1. Copy the two changed files into your real home directory.\n2. Reload the job with `launchctl bootout`, then `launchctl bootstrap`.\n3. Run `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`.\n\nThen check that the Telegram message arrives and that the run takes a plausible time.\n\nTwo things I couldn't confirm:\n- If `claude` lives in `~/.local/bin`, add that to the plist `PATH`.\n- I assumed `notify.sh` can read its token from the keychain under launchd.\n\nThe causes and fixes are written up in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":528,"cache_read_input_tokens":26258,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":528},"output_tokens":568,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":